# What a build context rooted at this repository must not carry.
#
# docker/fuzz/fuzz.sh is the only build here whose context is the repository root - the
# release builds under docker/build/ use their own directory - and its Dockerfile copies
# four things: the vcpkg manifest, the vcpkg configuration, the overlay triplets and one
# script. BuildKit already sends only what a COPY names, so this file is not what makes
# the context small.
#
# It is here for the other reason. This tree holds material that must never leave the
# machine, and a build context is a copy of a directory into a daemon - a second way for
# it to travel that .gitignore has nothing to do with. AGENTS.md: gitignored is not a
# guarantee, it is a default that a new directory gets around. So the held trees are named
# explicitly, and named here as well as there.
trail-data/
corpus/local/
corpus/blobs/
corpus/shards/
docs/local/

# Build output and caches: large, machine-specific, and rebuilt inside the container.
build/
build-release/
build-static/
build-win-release*/
vcpkg_installed/
fuzz/work/
.git/
.vcpkg-cache*/
dist/
